  "interpretation": "<p>Peripheral Blood Smear test is a type of blood test that involves looking at a sample of blood under a microscope to examine the appearance and characteristics of the blood cells.</p><ul><li>RBC: Changes in the appearance of the RBCs can indicate anemia or other medical conditions.<br></li><li>WBC: Changes in the number or appearance of the WBCs can indicate an infection, inflammation, or other medical conditions.<br></li><li>Platelets: An abnormal number or appearance of the platelets can indicate bleeding disorders or other medical conditions.<br><br></li></ul>",
